_id": "toolu_013kXTGHrhGXZ4jRNZqzbngz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49738, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013kXTGHrhGXZ4jRNZqzbngz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 51566, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QfqNMZPwMbHLDdCp8bJP4j", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51866, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QfqNMZPwMbHLDdCp8bJP4j", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51866, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QfqNMZPwMbHLDdCp8bJP4j", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54727, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, which left the regions mixed. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The first attempt to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It showed the incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary describes the rollback and the partial failure.\n\nStill open: the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt. v2.3.1 has not been redeployed, and no further deploys were made.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KgMdmKWCe6P9sXbBNknKRQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01M1niFcaztexhj9XDn2n8jq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production and is currently live in all three regions. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01S18StBeun84qR3PraV7X2d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KGLqKydQXFVMHjUihwzAXe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DisbAXPjGFA824DCpyKszg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped after us-east, so us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback to v2.3.0 to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DDMvi5w7FFdc7twTkJYcEt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014Af2jKT78LsshQpmBV2F6p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013kXTGHrhGXZ4jRNZqzbngz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 is older). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west all on v2.3.0). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production and has not been redeployed. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QfqNMZPwMbHLDdCp8bJP4j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, which left the regions mixed. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The first attempt to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It showed the incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary describes the rollback and the partial failure.\n\nStill open: the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt. v2.3.1 has not been redeployed, and no further deploys were made.", "type": "text"}]}]}